+# Skill Lens 0.2 — Why Resolution Screen Walkthrough (U4)
+
+> **Status:** Implemented by Gemini 3.8 Flash High through Antigravity under explicit owner authorization.
+> Independent reviews by MiniMax M3.1 Flash and DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 pending; Sol coordinates/accepts.
+> Human visual approval and 0.2 publishing are not claimed.
+> **Scope:** Full-Screen TUI Assignment U4 (`FULL_SCREEN_TUI.md` §§8.4, 9.1, 21.7 and 22 U4).
+> **Reference Plan:** [docs/plans/2026-10-26-tui-u4-why.md](plans/2026-10-26-tui-u4-why.md)
+> @ frozen commit `684cdb7aa0e3a28e5bb722bf65e4f3953edc6f76`.
+> **Implementing base:** `main` @ `1b01d9e14969e93456faa4146cced863a435ef4a`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. What changed, in plain English
+
+U3 delivered the Home browsing screen, which presents the catalog of installed skills with inline preview and agent cycling. U4 delivers the dedicated **Why Resolution Screen** (`WhyScreen`), accessible by pressing `Enter` on a focused, nonempty Home skill row.
+
+The Why screen provides complete insight into how an agent resolves candidate skill entrypoints for a specific skill:
+1. **Header & Context:** Displays canonical installation path, skill name, active working directory, selected agent, lookup skill name, collision policy (and documented policy evidence), and the report-wide headline.
+2. **Agent Switching Strip:** An interactive button strip at the top allows switching between all registered agents eligible for the selected skill. Switching agents can also be done via `Left` and `Right` keys when the strip is focused.
+3. **Candidate Collapsibles:** Every candidate considered during resolution is presented in a keyboard-accessible Textual `Collapsible` widget in deterministic resolution order. The candidate corresponding to the selected installation (matching the opening installation key) is initially expanded by default, while shadowed or alternate candidates remain collapsed.
+4. **Honest Status & Error Reporting:** Dedicated status widgets (`#why-status`, `#why-error-details`, `#why-report-status`) separate background engine lifecycle from report loading state and internal faults. If a background scan refresh finishes while the detail screen is open, the detail screen transparently re-derives its entry from the new snapshot without discarding active report content; if the installation was removed during refresh, the detail screen closes back to Home and displays a persistent removal notice.
+5. **Exact Token Lifecycle & Zero Live Reads:** Detail screens maintain explicit token identity for asynchronous report requests. An unmount or agent switch cancels only the detail's own active request, never invalidating resumed Home tokens or unrelated workers. Live filesystem reads are completely forbidden; detail rendering operates strictly on the frozen `SessionSnapshot` and immutable `ResolutionReport`.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Delivered files and responsibilities
+
+| File | Change |
+| --- | --- |
+| `skill_lens/tui/why.py` | New (824 lines). Implements `WhyScreen(Screen[None])`, `_WhyHost` protocol, pure helpers (`_eligible_agent_options`, `_unavailable_agent_ids`, `_entry_for_key`, `_build_candidate_blocks`), agent button strip, collapsible candidate container, pre-dispatch UI validation, exact token lifecycle management (`_cancel_owned_token`), and strict literal rendering (`markup=False`). |
+| `skill_lens/tui/home.py` | Integrated `HomeScreen`: bound `DataTable.RowSelected` and `action_open_why` so Enter opens `WhyScreen` only on a focused nonempty table; explicit `suspend_why` guards against hidden selection/sync/filter/drive mutations; `resume_why` and `on_screen_resume` restore Home table focus and sync upon returning; persistent `#removal-notice` displays removal feedback until explicit navigation. |
+| `skill_lens/tui/app.py` | Implemented `open_why` and `close_why` with exact token cleanup before pop and Home resumption; active-screen status queries target `#why-status` / `#why-error-details` on `WhyScreen` vs `#status-text` / `#error-details` on `HomeScreen`; report outcome notifications route to the current browsing screen with controller-accept first. |
+| `skill_lens/tui/__init__.py` | Exported `WhyScreen`. |
+| `tests/test_tui_why.py` | New (2066 lines, 36 tests): comprehensive event-controlled tests covering navigation, double-Enter deduplication, backspace/escape returns, agent strip switching, defensive unknown/zero-agent explanations, token ownership isolation, agent switch races, cache hits, sticky report faults, refresh survival and removal, candidate collapsibles, literal rendering (`markup=False`), narrow 60x24 layout, target preservation sentinels, and unit branch coverage. |
+| `docs/TUI_U4_WALKTHROUGH.md` | This document. |
+| `docs/validation/u4/implementation/mutation_gate.py` | Reproducible mutation harness verifying that 5 planted defects in `why.py` are caught by test assertions on a disposable copy outside the checkout. |
+| `docs/validation/u4/implementation/mutation_gate.json` | Machine-readable mutation receipt. |
+
+---
+
+## 3. Key Invariants & Architecture
+
+### 3.1 Enter Key Routing & Focus Invariants
+- On `HomeScreen`, `Enter` on the filter `Input` submits the filter without opening the detail screen.
+- `Enter` on the `DataTable` triggers `DataTable.RowSelected` only when the table is nonempty and has focus, invoking `open_why`.
+- On an empty table or filtered empty state, pressing `Enter` is a safe no-op.
+- Double-pressing `Enter` does not mount duplicate Why screens.
+- Pressing `Escape` or `Backspace` on `WhyScreen` pops the screen and returns to Home, fully preserving Home's filter text, cursor position, selection, and table focus.
+
+### 3.2 Suspension & Exact Token Lifecycle
+```
+[Home Screen (Active)]
+     │
+     │ user presses Enter on table
+     ▼
+[Home: suspend_why()] ── guards all hidden sync, drive, selection, filter
+     │
+     ▼
+[App: push_screen(WhyScreen)]
+     │
+     ▼
+[WhyScreen Mounted] ── pre-dispatch validation of (canonical_key, agent_id)
+     │
+     │ agent switch or close requested
+     ▼
+[Why: _cancel_owned_token()] ── exact token ownership check: active == owned
+     │
+     ▼
+[App: pop_screen()]
+     │
+     ▼
+[Home: resume_why() / on_screen_resume()] ── reconciles snapshot & restores focus
+```
+- In Textual, screen pop is asynchronous: `_cancel_owned_token` runs before `pop_screen`, ensuring stale detail workers do not deliver results into a resumed Home screen.
+- Only if the controller's active request matches the detail's owned token (`active == owned`) does detail cancellation invalidate the controller slot. An unowned token (such as a newly dispatched Home token) is never canceled.
+
+### 3.3 Candidate Collapsibles & Literal Rendering
+- Every candidate from `ResolutionReport.candidates` is mapped to a `Collapsible`.
+- Title displays: `[▾/▸] [*|x|?] <name> (<STATE>)` using Textual's `Content.from_text(..., markup=False)` to guarantee brackets, backslashes, and style tags render literally without markup interpretation.
+- Body displays: state mark and name/variant, canonical path, entrypoint path (when distinct from canonical location), content hash, reason, rule ID and evidence type, and report notes.
+- The candidate matching the selected installation canonical key is initially expanded by default; all others are collapsed.
+- If no candidates match, an explicit notice (`#why-no-match-notice`) informs the user.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Quality Gates & Verification Evidence
+
+All four verification gates pass cleanly on the finished tree:
+
+1. **Test Suite:**
+   ```bash
+   .venv/bin/pytest --cov=skill_lens
+   # 1121 passed, 1 expected case-insensitive-filesystem skip in 103.54s
+   # Combined coverage: 90.89% (floor: 90.0%)
+   # skill_lens/tui/why.py coverage: 90% (floor: 85%)
+   # skill_lens/tui/home.py coverage: 90%
+   ```
+2. **Type Checking:**
+   ```bash
+   .venv/bin/mypy
+   # Success: no issues found in 39 source files
+   ```
+3. **Linter & Formatter:**
+   ```bash
+   .venv/bin/ruff check skill_lens tests docs/validation/u4/implementation/mutation_gate.py
+   .venv/bin/ruff format --check skill_lens tests docs/validation/u4/implementation/mutation_gate.py
+   # All checks passed; 361 files already formatted
+   ```
+4. **Coordinator Reproduction Probe:**
+   ```bash
+   .venv/bin/pytest -p tests.conftest docs/validation/u4/implementation/coordinator/reproduction_r1.py
+   # 2 passed in 0.87s
+   ```
+5. **Mutation Harness:**
+   ```bash
+   .venv/bin/python docs/validation/u4/implementation/mutation_gate.py --out docs/validation/u4/implementation/mutation_gate_r2.json
+   # 5/5 mutants killed; 0 surviving; restored copy identical.
+   ```

